course: dictionary
lesson: 14104
title: Merged: joined into one
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When two or more things join together to become one thing, we say they have merged. Merged is the past form of merge, which means to join together into one. «The two rivers merged to form one wide river.» The rivers did not stay two separate rivers. They became one.
explain: Merged can also describe something that is already joined. «The merged class had twenty children from two different classes.» Merged tells you the class was made by joining two classes. Look at the words near it to find out what has joined.
explain: Check your meaning by putting «joined together into one» in place of merged. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right. «The paint colours merged to make purple.» Joined together into one makes sense here, so merged means joined into one.
fact: Merge means to join together into one.
fact: Merged is the past form of merge, so it tells you something has already joined.
fact: Merged can also be an adjective, as in «a merged class», which is a class made by joining two or more groups.
fact: «The two small schools merged into one big school.» The two schools became one school.
fact: Clue words like «together», «into one» and «joined» can help you spot merged in a sentence.
exercise: «The two streams merged into one river.» What does merged mean? | Ran very fast | Split apart into many | Dried up completely | *Joined together into one
exercise: In maths, «the two groups were merged to make one group of 12.» What does merged mean here? | Measured by weight | Counted separately | Taken away from each other | *Joined into one group
exercise: «The two colours merged to make green.» Find and copy the word that means joined into one. | colours | separate | green | *merged
test: «The two villages merged to form one town.» What does merged mean? | Grew smaller | *Joined together into one | Moved far away | Argued loudly
test: In «a merged class», what does merged tell you about the class? | It was split into two | It had no children | *It was already joined from two classes | It was painted blue
exam: What does merged mean in «The two streams merged and flowed on as one river»? | Divided | *Joined into one | Stopped flowing | Turned to ice
